WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.577
Cleaning is not finished when the code stops producing errors.

00:00:03.577 --> 00:00:05.947
We need to verify the result.

00:00:05.947 --> 00:00:10.927
This example starts with a cleaned DataFrame and performs several checks.

00:00:10.927 --> 00:00:13.252
We print the number of rows.

00:00:13.252 --> 00:00:16.092
We count duplicated order IDs.

00:00:16.092 --> 00:00:19.197
We count the total number of missing values.

00:00:19.197 --> 00:00:23.347
Then we keep only completed orders and summarize them by channel.

00:00:23.347 --> 00:00:27.542
Finally, we calculate total revenue as another check.

00:00:27.542 --> 00:00:30.332
Click Run and inspect each part.

00:00:30.332 --> 00:00:33.187
Validation should answer questions such as: did we accidentally duplicate records?

00:00:33.187 --> 00:00:35.972
Did we remove more rows than expected?

00:00:35.972 --> 00:00:38.727
Are required fields still missing?

00:00:38.727 --> 00:00:45.442
Does the grouped revenue equal the total revenue from the filtered table?

00:00:45.442 --> 00:00:49.782
These checks can catch errors before the data is used in a dashboard, statistical analysis,

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:54.162
or machine-learning model. A professional notebook should not only produce results.

00:00:54.162 --> 00:01:01.202
It should contain evidence that the results are based on data that still follows the assumptions of the

00:01:01.202 --> 00:01:02.878
analysis.
